cratic, a narrow Democratic edge in a genuine toss-up is the best read.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling this month, a shift in the national environment, or a late surge of Askar self-funding could move the race in either direction.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 50 days old; polling uncertainty inflated."]}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd District is an open seat that leans Republican by about four points, but a favorable national environment for Democrats has pulled the race back to roughly even. The nominees are both political newcomers: Republican Casey Askar, a Naples businessman who largely financed his own primary campaign, and Democrat Pia Dandiya, an educator who posted the stronger third-quarter fundraising haul.\n\nPublic polling is sparse and dated, with the latest survey from late August showing a two-point race, and both usable polls came from Democratic sponsors. Dandiya enters the final weeks with about $1.1 million on hand plus backing from the DCCC and Everytown, while Askar has under $100,000 in cash after heavy spending. Most race raters call the contest a toss-up, with a few tilting to each side, and prediction markets give Democrats a modest edge. The forecast lands on a narrow Democratic tilt in a genuinely competitive race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5455, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5764, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5967, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5933, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5824, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-10